                <pb facs="0948" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.00/153</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manchester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                        1925.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 27.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 766</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to your note of
                    the 22nd instant on Chinese affairs and to convey to you an expression of the
                    gratification felt by His Majesty’s Government at the agreement reached between
                    the Governments of the United States and Japan in regard to the proposed reply
                    to the Chinese note. While in the opinion of my Government the American draft
                    embodying the British and Japanese modifications is not wholly suitable for an
                    identic note, His Majesty’s Representative at Peking has been instructed to
                    confer with his American Colleague with a view to reaching a definite
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Chilton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
